/ `as TEXT` (uppercase) → case-insensitive at the parser→factory boundary.
/ Type.Name lowercases to "text". A literal's spelling is not its kind, so
/ the .md extension does NOT become a kind here (kind only from `as text/<kind>`
/ or a producing action).
Start
- set %x% = "readme.md" as TEXT
- assert %x.Type.Name% equals "text"
- assert %x.Type.Kind% is null
